[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Dynamic Component Loading in Angular"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Dynamic component loading is a powerful technique in Angular that allows you to add components to your application at runtime, rather than being statically defined in your templates. This is particularly useful for scenarios like displaying modal dialogs, loading plugins, or creating highly customizable user interfaces."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Key Concepts"},{"order":4,"type":"bullet_point","text":"**ComponentFactoryResolver:**  A service that is used to create component factories. A ComponentFactory is used to create instances of components."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"**ComponentFactory:**  A factory for creating a component. It contains the component's selector, inputs, and outputs."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"**ViewContainerRef:** Represents a container where one or more views can be attached. It provides methods for creating, inserting, and removing views."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"**NgModule:** Angular modules help organize an application into cohesive blocks of functionality."},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Step-by-Step Implementation"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"Let's walk through a practical example of dynamically loading a component. We'll create a simple 'AdBannerComponent' that can display different advertisements."},{"order":10,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Create the Dynamic Component"},{"order":11,"type":"code","text":"import { Component, Input } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-ad-banner',
  template: `<div class="ad-banner">{{data.message}}</div>`,
  styles: [".ad-banner { border: 1px solid black; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; }"]
})
export class AdBannerComponent {
  @Input() data: any;
}"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"This is a simple component that takes 'data' as input and displays a message."},{"order":13,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Create a Host Component"},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"import { Component, ViewChild, ViewContainerRef, ComponentFactoryResolver, AfterViewInit } from '@angular/core';
import { AdBannerComponent } from './ad-banner.component';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-ad-host',
  template: `<div class="ad-host"></div>`,
  styles: [".ad-host { border: 2px dashed gray; padding: 20px; }"]
})
export class AdHostComponent implements AfterViewInit {
  @ViewChild('adHost', { read: ViewContainerRef }) adHost!: ViewContainerRef;

  constructor(private componentFactoryResolver: ComponentFactoryResolver) { }

  ngAfterViewInit(): void {
    this.loadComponent();
  }

  loadComponent() {
    const componentFactory = this.componentFactoryResolver.resolveComponentFactory(AdBannerComponent);

    this.adHost.clear();

    const componentRef = this.adHost.createComponent(componentFactory);
    (<AdBannerComponent>componentRef.instance).data = { message: 'Welcome to our Ad!' };
  }
}"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"Explanation: 
- '@ViewChild' gets a reference to the DOM element where we want to insert the dynamic component.
- 'ViewContainerRef' represents the container where we can attach views.
- 'ComponentFactoryResolver' is used to resolve the 'ComponentFactory' for our 'AdBannerComponent'.
- 'loadComponent' method creates the component and sets the input 'data'."},{"order":16,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Template of the Host Component"},{"order":17,"type":"code","text":"<div class="ad-host" #adHost></div>"},{"order":18,"type":"paragraph","text":"The '#adHost' is a template reference variable that we use in the component to get a reference to the 'ViewContainerRef'."},{"order":19,"type":"subheading","text":"4. Declare the Dynamic Component in the Module"},{"order":20,"type":"code","text":"import { NgModule } from '@angular/core';
import { BrowserModule } from '@angular/platform-browser';
import { AdBannerComponent } from './ad-banner.component';
import { AdHostComponent } from './ad-host.component';

@NgModule({
  declarations: [
    AdBannerComponent,
    AdHostComponent
  ],
  imports: [
    BrowserModule
  ],
  entryComponents: [
    AdBannerComponent
  ],
  providers: [],
  bootstrap: [AdHostComponent]
})
export class AppModule { }"},{"order":21,"type":"paragraph","text":"Important: You must add the dynamically loaded component ('AdBannerComponent') to the 'entryComponents' array in your module. This tells Angular that this component will be created dynamically."},{"order":22,"type":"subheading","text":"5. Using the Host Component"},{"order":23,"type":"paragraph","text":"Now you can use the 'AdHostComponent' in your main application template:"},{"order":24,"type":"code","text":"<app-ad-host></app-ad-host>"},{"order":25,"type":"subheading","text":"Explanation"},{"order":26,"type":"paragraph","text":"This setup allows you to dynamically load 'AdBannerComponent' into the 'AdHostComponent'. The 'ComponentFactoryResolver' finds the factory for 'AdBannerComponent', and the 'ViewContainerRef' provides the location where the component is inserted. The 'entryComponents' array in the module ensures that Angular knows about the dynamically loaded component."},{"order":27,"type":"subheading","text":"Advanced Scenarios"},{"order":28,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Loading components based on user input or configuration."},{"order":29,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Creating a plugin architecture where components are loaded from external sources."},{"order":30,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Implementing modal dialogs or other UI elements that are created and destroyed dynamically."},{"order":31,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":32,"type":"paragraph","text":"Dynamic component loading is a powerful feature in Angular that enables you to create flexible and extensible applications. By understanding the core concepts and following the steps outlined in this tutorial, you can effectively leverage dynamic component loading in your projects."}]
